{ Your knight has just landed on g5. This time he checks first, and the check also hits your knight on b5. }
12... Qa5+ { Check, and the knight on b5 is attacked. Every block must be counted. } 13. Nc3 { The one block that saves the knight: it comes home from b5 with a hit on his queen. } (13. Kf1 { The king steps and the knight goes with check. } 13... Qxb5+ 14. Kg1 Nd7 { A piece down, and your rook on h1 is out of the game. [%csl Rh1] }) (13. Qd2 { The queen blocks and the knight is lost. } 13... Qxb5 { Gone. [%cal Ra5b5] }) (13. Bd2 { The bishop blocks and the knight is lost. } 13... Qxb5 { Gone. [%cal Ra5b5] }) (13. Ke2 { The king walks into the open. } 13... Qxb5+ { Check, and a piece down. [%cal Rb5e2] }) 13... h6 { Now the kick. Where does the knight go? Your bishop is guarded now, so count. } 14. Ne6 { Forward, into the fork square. You are back in the previous chapter: he takes on c3 and you win the fight. [%csl Ge6] } (14. Nf3 { Back home. Now the bishop is guarded, but watch the long diagonal. } 14... Bxc3+ 15. bxc3 Qxc3+ 16. Bd2 Rxe4+ { He picks up the bishop with check anyway. [%cal Re8e4] }) (14. Nxf7 { The hit on f7 comes too early. } 14... Bxc3+ 15. bxc3 Rxe4+ { Check, and the knight on f7 falls next. You are worse. [%cal Re8e4] }) (14. O-O { You give the knight for two pawns and safety. } 14... hxg5 15. Bc2 Qd8 { Roughly level. The knight to e6 kept the extra piece. }) (14. Bd2 { A quiet move; he simply takes the knight. } 14... hxg5 15. O-O Qd8 { Two pawns for the piece. Level at best. }) 1-0


